it the cell cycle: analysis of patterns of cell production in pigmented and albino retinae.</article-title><source>J Comp Neurol</source><year>1999</year><volume>405</volume><fpage>394</fpage><lpage>405</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10076934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kralj-Hans</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Tibber</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jeffery</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mobbs</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differential effect of dopamine on mitosis in early postnatal albino and pigmented rat retinae.</article-title><source>J Neurobiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16187306</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cernak</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoica</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Byrnes</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Di Giovanni</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Faden</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of the cell cycle in the pathobiology of central nervous system trauma.</article-title><source>Cell Cycle</source><year>2005</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>1286</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16082214</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Herrup</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cell division in the CNS: protective response or lethal event in post-mitotic neurons?</article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><year>2007</year><volume>1772</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>66</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17158035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stroeva</surname><given-names>OG</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitashov</surname><given-names>VI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Retinal pigment epithelium: proliferation and differentiation during development and regeneration.</article-title><source>Int Rev Cytol</source><year>1983</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>221</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6315626</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="book">Mann I. The development of the human eye. Grune &#x00026; Stratton, New York: 1964.</citation></ref><ref id="r20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ishibashi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tian</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Handa</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Similarity of mRNA phenotypes of morphologically normal macular and peripheral retinal pigment epithelial cells in older human eyes.</article-title><source>Invest Ophthalmol Vis Sci</source><year>2004</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>3291</fpage><lpage>301</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15326154</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tibber</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Whitmore</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Jeffery</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cell division and cleavage orientation in the developing retina are regulated by L-DO